  "audit": "The floor ends at the lathe, workbench and tent; there is no route behind those objects. Preserve that boundary. Cut the near timber doorway, its two posts, buffer timbers and near lantern. The rail bed is floor; the buffer body is already blocked. The near crate stack and tent-side chest are also cut out; their small lower faces extending beyond the old rectangles are solid. Tile review: restore 21 floor tiles behind foreground silhouettes; block 0 occupied tiles. Every changed tile is listed below with its previous value and reason. Silhouettes replaced with full-resolution SAM ViT-H object masks; see sam_source and per-piece prompts. SAM silhouette review restores 28 additional reachable floor tiles: floor behind the raised barrel/crate stack; its ground bases stay blocked below this back approach.",
